  "raw_text": "Step 1: Express the vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\) as a linear combination of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nLet \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = x \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + y \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nThis gives us the system of equations:\n\\[3x - 5y = -13,\\]\n\\[x + 2y = 3,\\]\n\\[2y = 4.\\]\n\nStep 2: Solve the third equation for \\(y\\).\n\\[2y = 4 \\implies y = 2.\\]\n\nStep 3: Substitute \\(y = 2\\) into the second equation to solve for \\(x\\).\n\\[x + 2(2) = 3 \\implies x + 4 = 3 \\implies x = -1.\\]\n\nStep 4: Verify the solution by substituting \\(x = -1\\) and \\(y = 2\\) into the first equation.\n\\[3(-1) - 5(2) = -3 - 10 = -13.\\]\nThe values satisfy all three equations.\n\nStep 5: Use the linearity of matrix multiplication to find \\(\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\\[\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} = \\mathbf{A} \\left( -1 \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} \\right) = -1 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nStep 6: Substitute the given values of \\(\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\\[-1 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\mathbf{A} \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = -1 \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} + 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nStep 7: Perform the scalar multiplications and addition.\n\\[-1 \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix},\\]\n\\[2 \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix},\\]\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7 \\end{pmatrix}}<|im_end|>",
